WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.067
The first cards prompt you to question hidden assumptions and unclear ownership

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:10.133
in a polished clause. Unlimited duties, assumed monitoring and automatic after-hours availability

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:15.200
can leave ownership and capacity unresolved.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.925
The repair cards ask who does what and what limits and acceptance

00:00:18.925 --> 00:00:22.450
apply. Explain your wording. Identifying an unknown is a useful finding, not

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.975
a failure.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.533
Finally, try the agreement against a change in time or place. If

00:00:30.533 --> 00:00:34.867
the revised work exceeds the accepted scope, obtain the necessary decision or

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:39.200
acceptance instead of relying on the old wording.
